WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.040
Sometimes we go to movies to laugh, sometimes
we go to cry, and sometimes we want to have

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.480
our minds melted.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.100
No medium like film can take you on a psychedelic
trip, make you question the nature of everything

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.840
around you, or get you inside the headspace
of the truly deranged — and it appears that

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.540
next year will bring a ton movies designed
to blow everyone's minds.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:24.150
Here are the 2018 movies that are bound to
be weird in the very best ways.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.240
Annihilation

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.840
Based on Jeff VanderMeer's 2014 novel, Annihilation
looks to be a crazy cinematic experience.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.579
The film follows an expedition to a place
called Area X, a portion of the Earth where

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:39.470
everything has gone wrong, and the laws of
physics no longer seem to apply.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:43.290
Previous missions to Area X have gone south
… eleven times over.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:48.030
Written and directed by Ex Machina's Alex
Garland, Annihilation will star Jennifer Jason

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:53.850
Leigh and Natalie Portman in this atmospherically
creepy film that hits theaters February 23rd.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.770
A Wrinkle in Time

00:00:55.770 --> 00:01:00.450
Madeleine L'Engle's 1962 young adult novel
A Wrinkle in Time has been blasting young

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.760
brains for generations.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.240
It's the story of precocious kids who must
rescue their dad from a fate worse than death

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.189
with the help of interdimensional beings Mrs.
Whatsit, Mrs. Who, and Mrs. Which.

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:15.719
The book's more surreal aspects have made
it difficult to adapt to a live-action production,

00:01:15.719 --> 00:01:20.369
but with Selma director Ava DuVernay and an
all-star cast, fans can expect an updated,

00:01:20.369 --> 00:01:24.689
yet faithful rendition of this otherworldly
classic when it debuts on the silver screen

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:26.590
March 9th.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:27.759
Ready Player One

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:31.819
Ernest Cline's novel Ready Player One had
secured a film deal before the book was even

00:01:31.819 --> 00:01:35.889
in stores, with Steven Spielberg anxious to
develop the story for film.

00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:40.460
The story centers on a virtual reality gamer
in a dystopian future who must run a gauntlet

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.079
of '80s pop culture-themed challenges while
looking for an Easter egg.

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:47.919
In the trailer alone, there were millions
of references, from The Iron Giant to Back

00:01:47.919 --> 00:01:49.679
to the Future to Freddy Krueger.

00:01:49.679 --> 00:01:54.390
Prepare for nerd culture overload when this
pic hits theaters on March 30th.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:55.719
Abruptio

00:01:55.719 --> 00:02:00.310
From writer/director Evan Marlowe comes Abruptio,
a thriller centered on a man who has a bomb

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.229
implanted in his neck and must do terrible
things to keep it from exploding.

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:05.880
As actor James Marsters explained:

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.170
"The lead character is feeding bodies into
a meat grinder.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.300
And that's not even the bad part.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.610
It's so bad."

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:17.280
If that's not strange enough, it'll also be
performed by life-sized latex puppets.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.610
We'll just have to wait to see whether it's
a work of genius, madness, or both when Abruptio

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:24.250
gets released on May 31st.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.330
Alita: Battle Angel

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:31.540
The live-action adaptation of the post-apocalyptic
manga and anime Battle Angel Alita has been

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:36.160
in the works since 2010, when the project
was brought to James Cameron's attention by

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.500
Guillermo Del Toro.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.920
Cameron had originally intended to direct,
but with his plate all full of Avatar sequels

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:45.860
for the next several years, that duty has
fallen to Robert Rodriguez.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:51.110
The cast is already stacked with talent like
Rosa Salazar, Jackie Earle Haley, Mahershala

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:53.960
Ali, Christoph Waltz, and Jennifer Connelly.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:58.350
And one of Cameron's signature filmmaking
strategies will live on with the film — since

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:03.240
Cameron only makes films that start with T
or A, it's now called Alita: Battle Angel

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.330
and will land in theaters on July 20th.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.920
Captive State

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.900
This sci-fi thriller has a cerebral concept:
what would your average neighborhood look

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:16.840
like a decade or so after an occupation by
a hostile force that just so happened to be

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.220
extra-terrestrial.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:22.660
Captive State will diverge from ordinary alien
fare to explore the human dynamics between

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.540
the dissidents and collaborator.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.490
With Rupert Wyatt of the modern Planet of
the Apes pics at the helm, you can count on

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:32.610
this one to be a disturbing hit when August
17th rolls around.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.050
Mortal Engines

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:38.310
Philip Reeves' The Mortal Engines books introduced
the post-apocalyptic concept of travelling

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:42.150
cities scouring a devastated earth and doing
battle with each other.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:46.760
Such a large-scale project seems untenable,
but with Peter Jackson co-scripting along

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:51.630
with his Lord of the Rings co-writers Fran
Walsh and Philippa Boyens, the project already

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.220
seems to be in good hands.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:57.459
Christian Rivers, who served as second-unit
director on all three Lord of the Rings films

00:03:57.459 --> 00:04:02.300
will make his feature film debut with the
pic, which drops on December 14th.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.220
The Endless

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.420
Filmmakers Aaron Moorhead and Justin Benson
have teamed up again after their 2012 thriller

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:12.720
Resolution to star as a pair of brothers who
have escaped the clutches of a cult, but are

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:16.450
compelled to return years later by a mysterious
tape sent in the mail.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:21.009
Early images from the film hint at a trippy
visual aesthetic, and the plot synopsis suggests

00:04:21.009 --> 00:04:24.949
that the cult's crazy otherworldly beliefs
maybe aren't so crazy after all.

00:04:24.949 --> 00:04:28.960
It all adds up to a project that just might
be worth keeping a close eye on, coming from

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.219
a pair of ambitious filmmakers who seem due
for a breakout hit.

00:04:33.219 --> 00:04:34.749
The House That Jack Built

00:04:34.749 --> 00:04:39.529
Not many filmmakers are as visually provocative
as Lars Von Trier, but his forthcoming The

00:04:39.529 --> 00:04:44.279
House That Jack Built has a truly unsettling
premise: it's an examination of the career

00:04:44.279 --> 00:04:48.599
of a serial killer who has been active for
more than a decade and who views each of his

00:04:48.599 --> 00:04:50.259
murders as a work of art.

00:04:50.259 --> 00:04:55.770
In the hands of Von Trier, such a story promises
a deep, dark psychological ride.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.169
Sorry To Bother You

00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:01.979
A story set in a surreal version of Oakland,
California, Sorry to Bother You is the story

00:05:01.979 --> 00:05:06.580
of a down-on-his-luck black telemarketer who
discovers a magical key to upward mobility

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:10.349
— the ability to make his voice sound like
a famous white actor.

00:05:10.349 --> 00:05:14.699
The film will mark the directorial debut of
legendary rapper Boots Riley of Oakland rap

00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:19.770
group The Coup, which has spent over two decades
making some of the most subversive music anyone

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:20.860
has ever heard.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.020
Keep an eye out for this one next year.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.240
The Man Who Killed Don Quixote

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:29.999
Perhaps no feature film has endured such a
rocky ride to screens as director Terry Gilliam's

00:05:29.999 --> 00:05:32.009
The Man Who Killed Don Quixote.

00:05:32.009 --> 00:05:36.229
His quest to get the film made long ago began
to mirror the foolish, futile endeavors of

00:05:36.229 --> 00:05:37.999
the classic literary character.

00:05:37.999 --> 00:05:41.840
But Gilliam's labor of love is finally coming
to theaters next year.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.440
The story focuses on an old man who believes
he is the legendary Quixote and mistakes a

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.650
confused advertising executive for his faithful
squire.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:53.699
He then proceeds to drag the man through a
time-jumping, mind-bending adventure where

00:05:53.699 --> 00:05:56.839
dreams and reality become tough to tell apart.

00:05:56.839 --> 00:05:57.839
Inversion

00:05:57.839 --> 00:06:02.290
The sci-fi thriller Inversion has two things
going for it right off the bat: Samuel L.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.419
Jackson and an insane premise.

00:06:04.419 --> 00:06:09.360
Jackson will portray a Homeland Security investigator
hot on the trail of an American con man and

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:14.539
a Chinese scientist who he thinks are responsible
for a whole new type of natural disaster — sudden,

00:06:14.539 --> 00:06:16.310
unexplained loss of gravity.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.409
The pic is sure to be a spectacle when it
falls into theaters next year.

00:06:20.409 --> 00:06:22.120
The Mandela Effect

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:26.409
Groupthink can be a strange thing, and "The
Mandela Effect" is a term meant to describe

00:06:26.409 --> 00:06:31.159
the effect of people collectively remembering
false events, like the death of Nelson Mandela

00:06:31.159 --> 00:06:36.029
in prison in the 1980s or Sinbad starring
in a movie about a genie.

00:06:36.029 --> 00:06:40.870
And for the record, no, really, neither of
those things happened...in our reality, at

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:41.870
least.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:45.659
Since memory is highly unreliable, it's an
effect to which almost anyone is susceptible,

00:06:45.659 --> 00:06:50.559
so co-writer and director David Guy Levy will
tap that trend for The Mandela Effect.

00:06:50.559 --> 00:06:54.779
The film will feature a man for whom the everyday
details of the world begin to change — and

00:06:54.779 --> 00:06:59.849
keep changing, until he starts to question
the nature of reality itself.

00:06:59.849 --> 00:07:01.099
Night on Bald Mountain

00:07:01.099 --> 00:07:06.229
Of all the Disney reboots in production, the
live-action adaptation of Night on Bald Mountain,

00:07:06.229 --> 00:07:10.879
the scariest, trippiest segment from Fantasia,
has somehow flown under the radar.

00:07:10.879 --> 00:07:15.430
The segment features a towering, demonic winged
creature called Chernabog that presides over

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:18.590
a night of festivities for a host of restless
spirits.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:21.860
The new version will focus on the backstory
of the demonic creature.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:25.789
You can depend on this pic to rekindle your
childhood nightmares next year.

00:07:25.789 --> 00:07:27.559
Thanks for watching!

00:07:27.559 --> 00:07:30.289
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:30.289 --> 00:07:32.610
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

